Preparing for a Senior Java Developer interview at Barclays?
If you have 3–5+ years of experience in Java, Spring Boot and Microservices, these are the kind of challenging questions you should be prepared to tackle.

1. Core Java – Deep Dive
What happens internally when two different keys generate the same hashCode() in a HashMap? At what point does a bucket transform into a Red-Black Tree?
Can a HashMap enter an infinite loop in a multithreaded environment? Explain the underlying reason.
If two objects have the same hashCode() but are not equal, can both exist as keys in a HashMap?
Can you override a static method in Java? What happens if the reference type and actual object type differ?
Why can a Java method be overloaded based on compile-time types but overridden based on runtime types?
What happens if a constructor calls an overridable method? What potential issue can arise?
Can a class be immutable if it contains a mutable object? How would you design it correctly?

2. Multithreading & Concurrency
Two threads update the same ConcurrentHashMap key simultaneously. How does Java handle the operation internally?
What is the difference between volatile and AtomicInteger? Can volatile guarantee thread safety for count++?
How can deadlock occur even when synchronised blocks are used correctly? How would you troubleshoot it?
What happens if CompletableFuture.thenApply() throws an exception? How would you recover without breaking the execution chain?
Difference between thenApply(), thenCompose() and thenCombine() with practical scenarios.
Your application has 200 threads, but only 10 database connections. What problems can occur, and how would you solve them?
Can a thread pool become exhausted even when CPU utilization is low?
How would you investigate a production issue where application threads are stuck in BLOCKED or WAITING state?

3. Java Streams & JVM
Why can a parallel stream perform worse than a sequential stream?
What happens if you modify a collection while processing it using a Stream?
Can you reuse a Java Stream after a terminal operation? What happens internally?
What is the difference between StackOverflowError and OutOfMemoryError?

4. Spring Boot & Hibernate – Tricky Scenarios
What happens if a @Transactional method calls another @Transactional method within the same class?
Why does @Transactional sometimes fail when applied to private methods?
What happens if two Spring beans depend on each other? How would you resolve circular dependencies?
How would you solve an N+1 query problem without blindly using FetchType.EAGER?
What happens if a transaction commits successfully but the application crashes before publishing its Kafka event?
